  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 sets no numeric permanent failure limit and never requires sales to stop. It only requires a corrective-action plan and retest above 5%, so Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%) is not forced off the market, and that section is the main gain for Northwind. Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9/100k) is subject to the mandatory 8-per-100k recall trigger in S5, but the text says a recall is not by itself a market ban. S4's 36-month suppression deadline is within the acceptable range and favours Halcyon's cost position, while the 6-year retrofit in S3 is within the acceptable range and favours Northwind's 38% shut-off coverage."
 },
